From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:23:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Supply the SD card
 from the PMIC

The SD card's vmmc is a fixed 3.3 V regulator. On the board VCC-CARD is
SWOUT2 of the AXP318W, the same switch output that feeds the eMMC.

Name SWOUT2 as the SD card's vmmc. It reports the 3.3 V of DCDC1, so the
OCR mask does not change, and it stays always-on. The fixed regulator
loses its last user and goes.

Not covered: UHS signalling. The SD card keeps 3.3 V I/O.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; mmc0 takes vmmc from
vcc-io, the DCDC1 voltage register in the PMIC reads back 3.3 V, and
both boards read 256 MiB from the SD card without errors.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts | 10 +---------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index b2cfae1c0449..fc2dcd3a0aec 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -57,14 +57,6 @@ scp@48100000 {
 			no-map;
 		};
 	};
-
-	reg_vcc3v3: vcc3v3 {
-		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
-		regulator-name = "vcc-3v3";
-		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
-		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
-		regulator-always-on;
-	};
 };
 
 &gmac0 {
@@ -96,7 +88,7 @@ ext_rgmii_phy: ethernet-phy@1 {
 };
 
 &mmc0 {
-	vmmc-supply = <&reg_vcc3v3>;
+	vmmc-supply = <&reg_swout2>;
 	cd-gpios = <&pio 5 6 (GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH | GPIO_PULL_DOWN)>; /* PF6 */
 	bus-width = <4>;
 	no-mmc;
